meta {
  name: Checkout
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/api/orders
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{customer_token}}
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "items": [
      { "product_id": {{product_id}}, "quantity": 1 }
    ],
    "shipping_name": "Budi Tester",
    "shipping_phone": "08123456789",
    "shipping_address": "Jl. Testing No. 1, Banjarbaru"
  }
}

docs {
  Before creating the order, this:
  1. Checks each product is published (product_display.is_published)
  2. Calls Accurate's item/detail.do LIVE for each item and rejects if
     requested quantity > availableToSell (422 "Insufficient stock")
  3. Prices from synced_items.unit_price — never trusts a client-sent price

  If Accurate itself is unreachable/erroring during the stock check,
  returns 503 rather than silently skipping validation.

  product_id here is a product_display.id (see "Catalog > List
  Products"), not an Accurate item id or SKU.
}
